# --- Generated run artifacts -------------------------------------------------
# Every run writes a timestamped set of netlists, ngspice raw files, result JSON
# and PNGs, and these are large (the working tree held ~120 MB of them before
# the first commit). main.py creates output/ on demand, so it needs no
# placeholder.
#
# The bare globs also cover runs pointed elsewhere with --out-dir. To commit a
# netlist deliberately, as a reference or a paper figure: git add -f <file>.cir
output/
*.raw
*.cir
*.out
*.out.[0-9]

# --- Input matrices (CSVs/) ---------------------------------------------------
# Excluded FOR NOW: the folder accrued a mix of deliberate example problems and
# ad hoc/debug scratch files, and they haven't been sorted yet. Once a curated
# subset is picked, add it back deliberately (git add -f CSVs/<file>.csv, or
# narrow/remove this rule) rather than re-adding the whole folder.
CSVs/

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# --- Virtual environments ----------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Tooling caches ----------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Editors and local agent settings ----------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# --- OS ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
